  "ref": "EZK.45.13",
  "review_notes": [
    "The second clause has no ordinal noun in Hebrew: שִׁשִּׁיתֶם itself means *give the sixth part of*, so *the sixth part* joins the verb's unit and the head sits on the complement (rule 44). A competing reading would leave *the sixth part* unattached, but no other morpheme licenses it."
